an="2" colspan="1">Feed conversion ratio<hr/></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Control</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.79 &#x000b1; 0.07 <xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijms-10-00001">(4)</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.18 &#x000b1; 0.07</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.54 &#x000b1; 0.09</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.47 &#x000b1; 0.02</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.06 &#x000b1; 0.58</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">DON<hr/></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.84 &#x000b1; 0.02<hr/></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.68 &#x000b1; 0.46<hr/></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.87 &#x000b1; 0.11<hr/></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.88 &#x000b1; 0.37<hr/></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.60 &#x000b1; 0.07<hr/></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn1-ijms-10-00001"><label><sup>(1)</sup></label><p>Before DON exposure;</p></fn><fn id="tfn2-ijms-10-00001"><label><sup>(2)</sup></label><p>Data are mean &#x000b1; SE of twelve (d-7 to d0), or six (others periods) pigs per group;</p></fn><fn id="tfn3-ijms-10-00001"><label><sup>(3)</sup></label><p>Data are mean &#x000b1; SE of consumption per animal per day, calculated on the basis of collected values in two pens per group (n=2);</p></fn><fn id="tfn4-ijms-10-00001"><label><sup>(4)</sup></label><p>Data are mean &#x000b1; SE, calculated for the period on the basis of collected values in two pens per group; DON-treated and control animals were compared by Student t test:</p></fn><fn id="tfn5-ijms-10-00001"><label>***</label><p>indicates statistically significant differences, <italic>P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t2-ijms-10-00001" position="float"><label>Table 2.</label><caption><p>Evolution of bacteria counts in faeces from pigs during the experimental period.</p><